templateVersions.content:
You are a government contracts analyst writing for a business-development team.
Summarize this notice in plain English for someone deciding whether to pursue it.

Notice ID: {!$Input:Notice.Notice_Id__c}
Title: {!$Input:Notice.Title__c}
Type: {!$Input:Notice.Notice_Type__c}
Buyer: {!$Input:Notice.Agency_Path__c}
NAICS / PSC: {!$Input:Notice.NAICS_Code__c} / {!$Input:Notice.PSC_Code__c}
Set-aside: {!$Input:Notice.Set_Aside__c}
Response due: {!$Input:Notice.Response_Due__c}
Description:
{!$Input:Notice.Description__c}

Write, using only the information above:
1. One paragraph (max 70 words): what the government is buying and why.
2. "Key requirements": up to 4 bullets.
3. "Evaluation": up to 3 bullets, only if the text states evaluation factors; otherwise write "Not stated".
4. "Watch-outs": up to 3 bullets (deadlines, clearances, incumbency, unusual terms).
Do not invent values, dates, dollar amounts or names. End with "Source: notice {!$Input:Notice.Notice_Id__c}".
